{#- #838, 28 Sep 2026. The operator: "we need prospektor.ai/integrations to
    exist, not only prospektor.ai/integrations/close - and it should be styled
    similarily to Close's. We should mention all the integrations we already
    have as well as a short description why Close users should care."

    Close's directory (close.com/integrations) is a title, a grid of cards
    with a mark, a name and one line, and a category rail. This is that in the
    site's own tokens, minus the rail: nine cards do not need one (the
    studio's own grid decided the same, CLAUDE.md → Less is more), so the
    category is the card's subtitle. The cards are one include, shared with
    the Close page's *More integrations*, and every line on them is what the
    studio's help says the connection does. Nothing here lists an app the
    studio's Connect your apps grid does not hold. -#}

{#- Keep your CRM (#1396, 17 Nov 2026): the head of the page is the one
    sentence the operator wanted said out loud, that Prospektor sits on top of
    whichever CRM a team runs, and under it the flow in one row, in the shape
    of shootpick.com's integrations page: what you sell, Prospektor, your CRM,
    your sales process. The note under it is what the studio's help says a
    push writes (docs/help/articles/share-a-pitch.md, connect-apps.md). -#}
<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-inner">
    <span class="tag">{% t %}integrations{% endt %}</span>
    <h1 class="page-h1">{% t %}Works with the CRM you have.{% endt %}</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      {% t %}Prospektor does not replace your CRM. It finds the companies that fit and
      sends each one in with its people, a deal and a note, so your sales process
      runs where it always has.{% endt %}
    </p>
  </div>
</header>

